From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cargt <tim.carney@cargt.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 11:35:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] board: cargt: imx8mp_00377: use USB2 (OSM-L USB_A) for
 fastboot

The OSM specification designates USB_A as the module's device-mode
(fastboot/download) port. The 00377 SOM wires the SoC's native USB2
controller to OSM-L USB_A, and native USB1 (with its SuperSpeed lanes)
to OSM-L USB_C. OSM-L USB_B is not connected on the SOM. This was
checked against SOM schematic 014-00377-FE (J1 connector sheet: USB2_D_P
on AC14 = USB_A_D_P, USB1_D_P/TX_P on D10/A8 = USB_C_D_P/SSTX_P).

board_usb_init()'s dwc3_device_data hardcoded .base = USB1_BASE_ADDR,
so the fastboot/mfgtools gadget came up on OSM-L USB_C instead of the
spec's USB_A. On the 00365 carrier that is the "C" Type-C port rather
than the "A" port. A carrier that only exposes USB_A as a device port
can never enumerate fastboot at all.

dwc3_nxp_usb_phy_init() and HSIO_GPR_REG_0_USB_CLOCK_MODULE_EN are
controller-agnostic, so only .base needs to change. TCPC port1
(I2C 0x51) already targets the USB_A port's PTN5110 (U17 on 00365
rev 05), so its UFP/DFP setup now matches the controller in use.

Add CARGT_IMX8MP_00377_FASTBOOT_USB2, default y, so a carrier that
deviates from the spec can switch back to USB1.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Cargt board specific]

Signed-off-by: Cargt <tim.carney@cargt.com>
---
 board/cargt/imx8mp_00377/Kconfig        | 12 ++++++++++++
 board/cargt/imx8mp_00377/imx8mp_00377.c |  4 ++++
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/board/cargt/imx8mp_00377/Kconfig b/board/cargt/imx8mp_00377/Kconfig
index 2622cd2..ca04f6e 100644
--- a/board/cargt/imx8mp_00377/Kconfig
+++ b/board/cargt/imx8mp_00377/Kconfig
@@ -48,4 +48,16 @@ config CARGT_IMX8MP_00377_FORCE_DRAM_BOOTSTRAP
 	  read/write their EEPROM correctly, not for normal production
 	  builds - it always pays the cost of up to N training attempts.
 
+config CARGT_IMX8MP_00377_FASTBOOT_USB2
+	bool "Use the SoC's native USB2 controller for the fastboot/mfgtools USB gadget"
+	default y
+	help
+	  The OSM specification designates the USB_A port as the module's
+	  device-mode (fastboot/download) port. The 00377 SOM wires OSM-L
+	  USB_A to the SoC's native USB2 controller; native USB1 (with the
+	  SuperSpeed lanes) goes to OSM-L USB_C, and USB_B is not connected.
+	  Say y to bring the fastboot/mfgtools gadget up on USB2 (USB_A), as
+	  the spec requires. Say n only for a carrier that deviates from the
+	  spec and needs the gadget on native USB1 (USB_C) instead.
+
 endif
diff --git a/board/cargt/imx8mp_00377/imx8mp_00377.c b/board/cargt/imx8mp_00377/imx8mp_00377.c
index 967d549..0b6e710 100644
--- a/board/cargt/imx8mp_00377/imx8mp_00377.c
+++ b/board/cargt/imx8mp_00377/imx8mp_00377.c
@@ -270,7 +270,11 @@ static struct dwc3_device dwc3_device_data = {
 #else
 	.maximum_speed = USB_SPEED_SUPER,
 #endif
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_CARGT_IMX8MP_00377_FASTBOOT_USB2)
+	.base = USB2_BASE_ADDR,
+#else
 	.base = USB1_BASE_ADDR,
+#endif
 	.dr_mode = USB_DR_MODE_PERIPHERAL,
 	.index = 0,
 	.power_down_scale = 2,
